From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OAN Messaging <messaging@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:45:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(otp): deliver consent OTPs by SMS through the OAN
 Messaging Service

When CONSENT_MANAGER_OAN_DELIVERY_ENABLED is on with a base URL and token, both OTP
providers send each issued code as one SMS (purpose otp, expiring with the code) and
report delivers = true, so OtpService no longer needs the log or bucket harness. A code
that cannot be handed to OAN raises OtpError, so the request is refused visibly (422 no
phone, 502 refused, 503 unavailable, 500 misconfigured) instead of waiting on a code
nobody received. The code and phone are never logged.

- services/otp_delivery.py: phone resolution (test map; a registry resolver plugs in at
  resolve_phone), text that always fits one SMS part, one idempotency key per code.
- oan_client/: the OAN Messaging client (contract 3.0.0), vendored unchanged apart from
  relative imports.
- otp_service.py, otp_consent_service.py: a send whose outcome is uncertain still counts
  against the resend cooldown and the send budgets (a resend keeps the new code).
- tests: 14 unit tests and 7 integration tests through the partner portal API.
